cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Banjul Researcher — paragraph-level search over the African Commission and Court"
message: >-
  Cite this software using the metadata below. Legal propositions and quoted
  paragraphs should additionally cite the decision itself.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Szoszkiewicz"
    given-names: "Łukasz"
    email: "l.szoszkiewicz@amu.edu.pl"
    affiliation: "Adam Mickiewicz University, Poznań"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6671-2893"
abstract: >-
  Banjul Researcher is a search engine over the decisions of the African
  Commission on Human and Peoples' Rights and the judgments, rulings, orders
  and separate opinions of the African Court on Human and Peoples' Rights,
  the Commission's general comments, principles and guidelines, concluding
  observations on State reports and resolutions, and the decisions and general
  comments of the African Committee of Experts on the Rights and Welfare of
  the Child (ACERWC),
  at the level of the numbered paragraph. It adds findings of violation
  extracted from the operative parts, a citation check, and unofficial
  English machine translations of decisions published only in French.
keywords:
  - "African Commission on Human and Peoples' Rights"
  - "African Court on Human and Peoples' Rights"
  - "African Charter on Human and Peoples' Rights"
  - "case law"
  - "human rights"
  - "legal information retrieval"
license: "PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/lszoszk/banjul-researcher"
url: "https://lszoszk.github.io/banjul-researcher/"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
